{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\nP='.plans/basic-test-proof-current-20260811T130218Z-current-fresh8-isolated-plan'\nS='/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T130218Z-current-fresh8/current/worker/planning'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$P\" current-state '\"\\\\\n  -p 2.1: \\\"The isolated benchmark workspace contains planning inputs only: benchmark-test.md, task-spec.md, worker-prompt.md, and session-id.txt. No repository application source was inspected because the future task is to create one new standalone HTML file and this proof is planning-only.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 2.2: \\\"The tagged repository-local planning skill came from /tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T130218Z-current-fresh8/current/worker/planning/SKILL.md, with its repository-local UI validation reference and REVIEWER.md read before planning.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$P\" desired-outcome '\"\\\\\n  -p 3.1: \\\"A future executor can create button-chain.html with one initial button. Each click on the current last button appends exactly one new button below it, and clicking the fourth generated button clears the document and shows the exact lowercase text finished with a visible white border.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 3.2: \\\"The durable plan is complete when implementation, automated behavior checks, direct browser-story validation, bug handling, and handoff evidence are each represented by atomic work units and non-empty artifacts.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$P\" approach '\"\\\\\n  -p 4.1: \\\"Create the standalone HTML document structure first, add the visible completion styling, implement append behavior scoped to the current last button, implement the fourth-generated-button completion path, add focused automated checks, then run the direct browser story.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 4.2: \\\"Keep markup, styling, behavior, automated testing, and browser validation as separate reviewable work units even though the future implementation may place markup, CSS, and script in one HTML file.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$P\" scope '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"In scope: creation of button-chain.html, one initial button, generated buttons appended below the current last button, no append from non-last buttons, completion on the fourth generated button, document clearing, exact finished text, visible white border, and verification evidence.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"Out of scope for this proof: creating, editing, opening, serving, inspecting, or testing any HTML; starting a browser, server, driver, or other execution tooling; adding framework dependencies; and changing any repository files outside the plan artifacts and session-id.txt.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$P\" affected-areas '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"Future affected implementation file: button-chain.html. Planned scopes inside that file are the document root markup, .completion-message style rule, appendButtonAfterLastClick behavior, and finishOnFourthGeneratedButton behavior.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"Future affected test/proof areas are a focused behavior test target for button-chain.html and one browser user story that exercises real button clicks from the initial state through completion.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$P\" constraints-and-decisions '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"Planning-only proof constraint: no HTML artifact may be created or tested in this benchmark run. Acceptance criteria are recorded for a later executor.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 7.2: \\\"Decision: use a standalone browser-native HTML, CSS, and JavaScript implementation with no external libraries so the behavior can be verified by opening the file in a browser later.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$P\" risks-and-open-questions '\"\\\\\n  -p 8.1: \\\"Risk: the phrase fourth generated button means the fourth appended button, not the fourth button overall; the plan records this interpretation explicitly in the work units and story.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 8.2: \\\"Open question for future execution only: exact visual dimensions of the white border are unspecified, so any clearly visible white border around the finished text is acceptable unless the user later chooses a stricter style.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --field \"$P\" plan '\"'UI affected' yes\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --field \"$P\" plan '\"'Rationale' 'The future task creates a user-facing HTML page and click interaction.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/create-ui-validation.sh\" \"$P\" '\"'Future local button-chain.html opened in a browser after implementation; prohibited during this planning-only benchmark.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-goal.sh\" \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation '\"'Button chain behavior implementation' 'Create the standalone HTML file with initial UI, completion styling, append behavior, completion behavior, and automated behavior-test coverage planned as separate atomic targets.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-goal.sh\" \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation '\"'Direct browser story validation' 'Verify the completed button chain through a real browser click sequence and record evidence that the required story passes with no open bugs.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --testing-requirement \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation yes '\"'The goal changes observable UI behavior and owns a downstream automated test work unit.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --testing-requirement \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation yes '\"'The goal is itself direct browser validation of the required user story.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$P\" W01 markup button-chain.html '\"'document body button chain root' N/A 'Create a valid standalone HTML document containing exactly one initial button in the body and a container/order that supports generated buttons below it.' '—' 01-button-chain-implementation 01-step-document-markup\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$P\" W02 style button-chain.html '\"'.completion-message' N/A 'Define the visible completion presentation for the exact text finished, including a visible white border.' W01 01-button-chain-implementation 02-step-completion-style\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$P\" W03 source button-chain.html '\"'appendButtonAfterLastClick' N/A 'Handle clicks so only the current last button appends exactly one new button directly below it.' W01 01-button-chain-implementation 03-step-append-last-button\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$P\" W04 source button-chain.html '\"'finishOnFourthGeneratedButton' N/A 'When the fourth appended/generated button is clicked as the current last button, clear the document and render only the completion state with exact lowercase text finished.' W02,W03 01-button-chain-implementation 04-step-fourth-generated-finish\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$P\" W05 test button-chain.html '\"'button-chain behavior test' N/A 'Add a focused automated test or scripted DOM check that proves initial state, exact one-button append per last-button click, ignored non-last clicks, fourth-generated completion, exact text, and white border style.' W01,W02,W03,W04 01-button-chain-implementation 05-step-behavior-test\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-work-unit.sh\" \"$P\" W06 verification N/A '\"'US-01 browser click flow' N/A 'Open the implemented file in a browser and use direct clicks on visible buttons from the initial state through the fourth generated button, confirming completion evidence and no unresolved bug rows.' W05 02-browser-story-validation 01-step-browser-story-us-01\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$P\" '\"'button-chain.html exists as the sole future implementation file with one initial button' W01 'The markup unit creates the standalone document and initial visible button.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$P\" '\"'pressing the current last button appends exactly one button below it' W03,W05,W06 'Behavior implementation, automated check, and browser story cover the append contract.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$P\" '\"'pressing the fourth generated button clears the document' W04,W05,W06 'Completion behavior is implemented and then verified by test and browser story.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$P\" '\"'completion prints exact lowercase finished with a visible white border' W02,W04,W05,W06 'Style, completion behavior, automated check, and browser story cover the final visual state.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-coverage.sh\" \"$P\" '\"'planning-only benchmark safety boundary is preserved' W06 'The plan records future browser verification but this run does not create or execute HTML.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/add-ui-story.sh\" \"$P\" US-01 '\"'Future user opening the completed standalone file from a fresh browser context' 'Click the initial button, click the first generated last button, click the second generated last button, click the third generated last button, then click the fourth generated last button.' 'Five direct mouse clicks or taps on visible button controls; each click targets the current last button in visual order.' 'After the fourth generated button is clicked, the document content is cleared and the only completion state shows exact text finished with a visible white border.' W01,W02,W03,W04,W05,W06\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/configure-ui-story-cache.sh\" \"$P\" US-01 '\"'Freshly opened implemented button-chain.html with one visible initial button and no generated buttons.' 'Mouse click or mobile tap sequence on visible button controls only.' 'Initial button, generated button 1, generated button 2, generated button 3, generated button 4.' 'After each of the first four clicks, exactly one additional button is visible below the previous last button; after the fifth click, finished is visible with a white border.' '2 seconds per append or completion readiness signal'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$P/01-button-chain-implementation\" 01-step-document-markup '\"'Automated check after implementation: open or parse button-chain.html and assert the body starts with exactly one visible button before any interaction; do not bundle behavior assertions into this markup step.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$P/01-button-chain-implementation\" 02-step-completion-style '\"'Automated style check after implementation: assert the completion element uses the .completion-message selector and its computed or declared border is visible and white.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$P/01-button-chain-implementation\" 03-step-append-last-button '\"'Automated behavior check after implementation: click only the current last button repeatedly and assert each eligible click appends exactly one new button below it; separately click a non-last button and assert it does not append.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$P/01-button-chain-implementation\" 04-step-fourth-generated-finish '\"'Automated behavior check after implementation: create four generated buttons through valid clicks, click the fourth generated button, and assert prior content is removed and exact text finished remains.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$P/01-button-chain-implementation\" 05-step-behavior-test '\"'Run the future automated test target and require all assertions for initial state, append behavior, non-last protection, fourth-generated completion, exact text, and white border to pass.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$P/02-browser-story-validation\" 01-step-browser-story-us-01 '\"'Browser verification after implementation only: open button-chain.html, perform the cached direct click sequence for US-01, capture visible evidence of finished with a white border, and record pass/fail plus any bug rows.'\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --decomposition-review \"$P\" completed\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
