{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\nP='.plans/basic-test-proof-current-20260811T130218Z-current-fresh8-isolated-plan'\nS='/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T130218Z-current-fresh8/current/worker/planning'\n# Finish goal narratives\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation affected-areas '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"Future file button-chain.html contains the planned markup selector #button-chain-root, the .completion-message style rule, and two named script behaviors: appendButtonAfterLastClick and finishOnFourthGeneratedButton.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"Future test target button-chain behavior test may be a lightweight browser/DOM script or project-appropriate automated check, but it must not change production behavior.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation dependencies-and-handoffs '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"W01 enables W02 and W03 by establishing the DOM root and initial button. W02 and W03 enable W04. W01 through W04 enable W05.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 7.2: \\\"Handoff to Goal 02: button-chain.html and its automated behavior check have passed locally, including exact finished text and visible white border assertions.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases '\"\\\\\n  -p 8.1: \\\"Use event handling that identifies the current last button at click time, so older generated buttons cannot append more buttons after they stop being last.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 8.2: \\\"Track generated button count separately from total button count so the fourth generated button means the fourth appended button; the initial button is not counted as generated.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 8.3: \\\"On completion, replace document body contents with one completion element using exact text finished and .completion-message styling.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation goal-size-exception '\"\\\\\n  -p 11.1: \\\"Not applicable; this goal owns five work units, within the 2-10 work-unit limit.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs '\"\\\\\n  -p 2.1: \\\"This goal starts only after Goal 01 hands off an implemented button-chain.html and a passing automated behavior check. During this benchmark proof the browser run remains planned and unexecuted.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation why-this-goal-is-needed '\"\\\\\n  -p 4.1: \\\"The requested behavior is a user-facing click flow; direct browser validation is the acceptance contract that proves the future implementation works through visible controls.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation scope '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"Included: one bounded story, US-01, using direct clicks or taps on the visible initial and generated buttons through the completion state.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"Excluded in this planning-only proof: opening the HTML file, running a browser, serving files, taking screenshots, or marking the story passed before future execution evidence exists.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation affected-areas '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"Future verification target is the rendered button-chain.html file. Plan artifacts affected during execution are ui-user-stories.md, ui-story-runs/US-01.md, and bugs.md if a story failure is found.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation dependencies-and-handoffs '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"Depends on W05 from Goal 01. If US-01 fails, execution must record the bug, add investigate/fix/retest work units before completion, and keep the original bug evidence.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 7.2: \\\"Completion handoff: US-01 has browser evidence showing finished with a visible white border, and bugs.md has no unresolved bug rows.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases '\"\\\\\n  -p 8.1: \\\"Run the cached sequence exactly: click the initial button, then generated buttons one through four as the current last button. Check the count after each append and final completion after the fifth click.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 8.2: \\\"If completion happens on the third generated button or requires a sixth click, treat it as a failing story and open the bug loop instead of weakening the story.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation goal-size-exception '\"\\\\\n  -p 11.1: \\\"Allowed single-work-unit goal: this is a standalone verification outcome, which the skill permits when the goal is genuinely verification-only.\\\"\n# Step details\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/01-step-document-markup instructions '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"Create button-chain.html as a valid standalone HTML document with a body-level root identified as #button-chain-root.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"Place exactly one initial visible button in the root. Do not add generated buttons, completion text, scripts beyond what later work units own, or external dependencies in this step.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/01-step-document-markup acceptance-criteria '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"button-chain.html exists after future execution and contains one initial visible button before any interaction.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"The root for the button chain is named #button-chain-root and supports appending generated buttons in visual order below the current last button.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/01-step-document-markup handoff '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"W02 and W03 can rely on a stable #button-chain-root and a single initial button target.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/02-step-completion-style instructions '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"Add only the .completion-message style rule in button-chain.html.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"Style must make the final finished text visibly bordered in white; choose simple dimensions such as a solid white border and enough padding for visibility.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/02-step-completion-style acceptance-criteria '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"A completion element using .completion-message will display a white border that is visibly distinguishable from its background.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"This step does not define click behavior or create completion content.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/02-step-completion-style handoff '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"W04 can apply .completion-message when replacing the document with the finished state.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/03-step-append-last-button instructions '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"Implement appendButtonAfterLastClick so a click is eligible only when the clicked button is the current last button in #button-chain-root.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"For each eligible non-completion click, append exactly one new button immediately below the previous last button and update generated-button state once.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.3: \\\"A click on any earlier button must leave the button count unchanged.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/03-step-append-last-button acceptance-criteria '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"Clicking the current last button before completion appends exactly one button below it.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"Clicking a non-last button after generated buttons exist appends zero buttons.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.3: \\\"This step does not clear the document or render finished; W04 owns that branch.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/03-step-append-last-button handoff '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"W04 can rely on an accurate generated-button count and last-button eligibility guard.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/04-step-fourth-generated-finish instructions '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"Implement finishOnFourthGeneratedButton as the completion branch for the fourth appended button when that button is clicked as the current last button.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"On completion, clear existing document content and render one completion state containing exact lowercase text finished with the .completion-message style.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.3: \\\"Do not count the initial button as generated; the completion trigger is generated button number four.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/04-step-fourth-generated-finish acceptance-criteria '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"After generated buttons one through four have been created, clicking generated button four clears previous buttons and content.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"The resulting document shows exact text finished in lowercase and has a visible white border.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.3: \\\"Completion does not occur before the fourth generated button is clicked.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/04-step-fourth-generated-finish handoff '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"W05 can test the full behavior from initial state through final completion.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/05-step-behavior-test instructions '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"Add one focused automated test target for button-chain.html using the project-appropriate lightweight browser or DOM test approach available during future execution.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"Assert initial one-button state, exactly one append per eligible current-last click, zero append from non-last clicks, completion only after clicking the fourth generated button, exact finished text, and visible white border styling.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/05-step-behavior-test acceptance-criteria '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"The future automated test fails if an eligible click appends zero or more than one button.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"The future automated test fails if completion happens on the wrong generated button, leaves old content behind, changes finished casing, or lacks a visible white border.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-implementation/05-step-behavior-test handoff '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"W06 may start after the automated behavior test has passed and its command/evidence are recorded by the executor.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation/01-step-browser-story-us-01 instructions '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"After implementation only, open the local button-chain.html in a browser and execute ui-story-runs/US-01.md exactly through visible mouse clicks or taps.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"Record the route or file URL, observed button counts after each append click, final finished text, visible white border evidence, and any console or rendering errors relevant to a failure.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.3: \\\"If any expected result fails, mark US-01 as bug found and populate bugs.md before adding investigation/fix work units.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation/01-step-browser-story-us-01 acceptance-criteria '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"US-01 is marked passed only after direct browser clicks produce the final finished state with a visible white border.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"bugs.md has no unresolved rows at completion, and the story cache contains actual evidence rather than planned-only placeholders.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$S/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$P\" 02-browser-story-validation/01-step-browser-story-us-01 handoff '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"Initiative handoff is ready when W06 evidence confirms the full user story and no open bug loop remains.\\\"\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
